4. Cardiovascular and cerebrovascular abnormalities:

1. Concomitant or previous history of central nervous system disease, including seizures, hemorrhagic/ischemic stroke, severe brain injury, dementia, Parkinson's disease, cerebellar disease, paralysis, aphasia, mental illness, disturbance of consciousness, unknown Cause coma, neuropathy, organic brain syndrome, etc.;
